[Music]  at the end of the last video I talked  about interaction between any two bodies  whenever two bodies interact each one of  them applies force onto the other but  how do the bodies interact interaction  between the bodies can be basically of  two types one in which the bodies are in  contact with each other and the other in  which they are not in contact with each  other the forces that result when the  bodies are in contact with each other  are called contact forces and the forces  that results between the bodies when the  bodies are not in contact are called as  non-contact forces it's easy to think of  contact forces but it's a little  difficult to think of non-contact forces  right yes there are some forces which  operate between objects even though the  objects are not in contact we will study  more about non-contact forces in the  future videos first we will discuss  contact forces suppose that you're  thirsty and there is a glass full of  water lying on the table in order to  drink some water from this glass you  have to lift the glass towards your  mouth that is you have to apply force on  the glass how are you applying this  force you are touching the glass with  your hand and lifting it here your hand  is in contact with the glass so the  force you are applying on the glass is  of contact force here is an example from  the previous video this player wants to  pass this football towards his teammate  who is standing on the other side of the  pitch the player will apply the force on  the ball by kicking it when the player  applies force his foot is in contact  with the football so this force is a  contact force  other examples of contact forces can be  pushing or pulling the desk from one  point to another point here our hands  are in contact with the desk  similarly pressing the keys on the  keyboard moving a piece on chess board  are some of the other examples in which  parts of a body are in  contact with the objects and applies  force on them in all the examples that  we've seen till now it is the paths of  the human body that are in contact with  the objects the forces generated due to  our body being in contact with the  object are called muscular forces the  muscles in our body expand and contract  when we apply force on objects animals  also use muscular force to carry out  their physical activities a bullock cart  is used to carry load from one point to  another Bullock's are tied with a cart  and the load is then added onto the cart  the bullet then applies muscular force  on the cart and moves it forward so the  muscular force is a contact force are  there any other contact forces other  than muscular force yes there are we  will see them in the next video  [Music]

